    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7767" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Chatti</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Catti</span></b> ), ōrum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χάττοι</span>, Strab., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a German people in the present Hesse</i>
			(which name is formed from Chatti) <i>and
			Thuringia</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. G. 30</span></i> Rup.; 31 sq.; <i><span class="en">id. A. 1,
				55 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. H. 4,
			12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 37</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 14,
				28, § 100</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 4,
				147 al.</span></i>—In sing.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Chatta mulier,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Vit. 14</span></i>
			.</div>
